Z||000000||Dan87GT||12-24-1999||03:47 PM||||Does anyone where I can purchase some "Safety" torx bits ,I need to remove my timing indicator and regular torx bits will not fit because of the "safety" pin that is in the center of the bolt<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||12-24-1999||03:50 PM||||Try your local tool discounter, MATCO or Snapon truck. You can also try here.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.jensentools.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.jensentools.com/</A> <P>They carry allot of specialty tools, mostly for the electronics and telecom industry.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||12-24-1999||04:27 PM||||Or take a small chisel or screwdriver and break the pin and use a regular torx bit. Or drill a hole in your torx bit.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bill Osmer||12-25-1999||07:58 PM||||Almost any auto parts store carries them now; the concept of "security" associated with them is a little thin  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||12-26-1999||11:17 AM||||Graniger has a nice set. Security bits ( It's on sale ) <A HREF="http://www.grainger.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.grainger.com</A>      I think thats it.||||reg||3
